  "question": {
    "text": "A hydrogen atom in its ground state absorbs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>eV</mi></math> of energy. The angular momentum of electron of the hydrogen atom will increase by the value of&nbsp;(Given, Planck&#39;s constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi>Js</mi></math>)."
  },
